  "id": "flicker-stimulus",
  "term": "flicker stimulus",
  "definition": "A flicker stimulus is a visual target that repeatedly flashes and is used to evoke steady-state visual responses for purposes such as brain-computer interface control. In the source, it refers to a flashing visual signal that a user looks toward or keeps in peripheral view so the system can extract control information from the brain response.",
